{
  "_note": "Mitochondrion: the Cortassa-Aon-Marban-Winslow-O'Rourke (2003) integrated model of cardiac mitochondrial energy metabolism and Ca2+ dynamics (Biophys J 84:2734). The TCA cycle, oxidative phosphorylation (ETC proton pumping, F1F0-ATPase, ANT, proton leak) and Ca2+ handling (uniporter, Na+/Ca2+ exchanger) are coupled through the inner-membrane potential delta-psi. Every value below is taken verbatim from the authoritative Physiome/CellML encoding of the model. Two documented curation fixes are applied in the code: the Na+/Ca2+ exchanger uses the [Ca]m/[Ca]i ratio (matrix efflux), and the F1F0 fluxes are signed for net ATP synthesis. A reactive-oxygen-species module (after Cortassa 2004 / Zhou 2009: shunt production, SOD scavenging, ROS-activated inner-membrane anion channel) and a permeability transition pore (Ca/ROS-gated, after Bernardi 2015 / Pokhilko 2006) use the published functional forms with calibrated parameters. Units: concentrations mM (Ca and its affinity constants uM), fluxes mM/s, potentials V, time s.",
